course: dictionary
lesson: 11562
title: Anatomical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anatomical is an adjective. It tells you that something is to do with the structure of a body: how its parts are made and how they fit together. Context helps: «The doctor showed us an anatomical model of a human heart.» The model shows the parts of the heart, so anatomical must mean to do with the body's structure.
explain: «Leonardo da Vinci made careful anatomical drawings of people and horses.» Those drawings show how bones, muscles and organs are arranged inside, not just how a body looks from outside. Swap in your meaning: "careful drawings to do with the body's structure" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «The science class labelled the anatomical diagram: skull, ribs and spine.» The labels name each part exactly. Anatomical words are precise, so you will meet them in science, sport and medicine whenever people need to name body parts clearly.
fact: Anatomical means to do with the structure of the body of a person, animal or plant.
fact: «An anatomical drawing» shows how the parts of a body are built and arranged.
fact: Anatomically correct means shaped like the real body.
fact: Leonardo da Vinci made famous anatomical drawings.
fact: Anatomical diagrams and models show bones, muscles and organs.
exercise: «The vet used an anatomical model to show how the dog's heart fits in its chest.» What does anatomical mean? | Very fast and loud | To do with the weather | *To do with the structure of a body | Covered in fur
exercise: Ruby says a plant can be anatomical too. Why might she be right? | Plants cannot be studied at all | Plants are always red | *Plants have a structure, with parts like roots, stems and leaves | Plants only grow in gardens
exercise: «The cartoon robot is not anatomically correct: it has wheels instead of legs.» What does anatomically correct mean? | Very cheap to buy | Painted in bright colours | *Shaped like the real body | Made of wood
test: Which word means to do with the structure of the body? | *Anatomical | Musical | Political | Tropical
test: «Mia drew a cat with every bone and muscle labelled.» Which word best describes her drawing? | Noisy | Rainy | Sweet | *Anatomical
exam: Dr Patel says, «This model is anatomically correct.» What does she mean? | It is made of paper | *It is shaped like the real body | It is very old | It is for sale
